      "title": "START HERE",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Fibo 2 Dev • pure text-to-image with boxes\n1. Draw/move/resize boxes in **Create Bounding Boxes**, then describe each object. Two example objects are provided. Draw background first, foreground last.\n2. Change **SCENE / STYLE** in the large text node to describe the overall setting and appearance. Use type **text** only for lettering you want rendered.\n3. Run. The Dev model uses 30 steps and CFG 5; results are saved under `Fibo2_t2i_layout/`.\n\nNo source image is needed. Only the box descriptions and coordinates enter Fibo; the layout image is a preview for you and is not passed to the model. Positioning is prompt guidance, not a hard regional constraint.\n\nCanvas and output are 1024 × 1024. If changing aspect ratio, change width/height in both Create Bounding Boxes and Fibo. Enable Nodes 2.0 if the canvas editor appears as a placeholder. To preview boxes without generating, temporarily mute Save Image."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Fibo 2 Dev • pure text-to-image with boxes\n1. Draw/move/resize boxes in **Create Bounding Boxes**, then describe each object. Two example objects are provided. Draw background first, foreground last.\n2. Change **SCENE / STYLE** in the large text node to describe the overall setting and appearance. Use type **text** only for lettering you want rendered.\n3. Run. The Dev model uses 30 steps and CFG 5; results are saved under `Fibo2_t2i_layout/`.\n\nNo source image is needed. Only the box descriptions and coordinates enter Fibo; the layout image is a preview for you and is not passed to the model. Positioning is prompt guidance, not a hard regional constraint.\n\nCanvas and output are 1024 × 1024. If changing aspect ratio, change width/height in both Create Bounding Boxes and Fibo. Enable Nodes 2.0 if the canvas editor appears as a placeholder. To preview boxes without generating, temporarily mute Save Image."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
